{
  "_comment": [
    "TV Thing's channel lineup v4.1, laid out like an old cable lineup card (lineup.py reads it).",
    "A channel is its source and its id there: an antenna channel by its virtual number (digital 22.4),",
    "a Roku feed by its YouTube TV row (youtube-tv NBC), an internet stream by its id (internet_streams.json).",
    "'name' renames it in the lineup; 'note' is for people reading this file and is ignored.",
    "0-9 are our own channels: VizelVision, its slide channels (source vizelvision with a channel, such as",
    "the Sports Guide on 6) and the in-house and web streams. A new web stream still lands in 370-379; it",
    "gets a single digit only when pinned here. 3-5 and 7-9 are held for more.",
    "Washington's locals: each network's last digit is its channel on the air (14 NBC 4, 15 FOX 5, 17 ABC 7,",
    "19 CBS 9), a station's second channel right after it, NHK first on 10.",
    "The Michigan block follows the Lansing and Flint dial (5, 6, 10, 12, 19, 23, 25, 47, 47.2, 53, 53.2, 66),",
    "so channel up runs as on an antenna there; the two markets never share a number. WSMH 66.2 is filed as 25,",
    "still branded NBC 25. YouTube TV's Lansing rows hold their stations' numbers until a Michigan antenna",
    "receiver exists; then the antenna stations take them and the YouTube TV copies move to 292-297.",
    "Held for it: 25 WNEM CBS 5.1, 28 WJRT ABC 12.1, 29 WDCQ PBS 19.1, 31 WSMH 66.2, 33 WSYM 47.2 (Pistons),",
    "36 WSMH FOX 66.1, 37-39 whatever its first scan finds, and 380-399 for its subchannels.",
    "Sports cable keeps its old order, moved up nine. 197 is Cairo Radio, a station slide channel.",
    "Games sections number each day's games by kickoff. A channel not listed here takes the first free number",
    "in the section whose 'new' names its source ('*' = any other), and keeps it in lineup_state.json; list it",
    "here to move it. 'hidden' channels are off the dial: no number, in no list, still tunable by id, their rows",
    "kept in roku.json and channels.json."
  ],
